 first-order initial value problem?\n\n- $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$\n- $8{y}^{′}-xy=3$\n- $3{y}^{″}=4y,\\,y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y$ together with the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\n- System II is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $3{y}^{″}=4y$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b65df1969efc25f29516062e2caa1a3c57e4f6191012bead8afceea49150b42e" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of those listed"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-118786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-95983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are third-order ordinary differential equations?\n\n- ${y}^{‴}+3x{y}^{′}=xy$\n- $3{y}^{″}{y}^{′}-2xy=2{y}^{′}$\n- ${x}^{3}{y}^{′}-2x={y}^{″}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-95983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differential equation is of third-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{‴}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is a third-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴}.$\n\n- Equation II is not a third-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is not a third-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-95983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "16df356ef31cec545731e1f9acaea88a42f029527110ece34371c9c2bae4b2cc"} {"question" "q-95983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-95983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of these listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-95983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\n- ${y}^{‴}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$\n- $5{y}^{″}{y}^{′}+3xy=4{y}^{′}$\n- ${({y}^{′})}^{2}-2{x}^{2}=y$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{′}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation II is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "16df356ef31cec545731e1f9acaea88a42f029527110ece34371c9c2bae4b2cc"} {"question" "q-96669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+5{y}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3{y}^{5}=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}},$ which has order $3.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "16df356ef31cec545731e1f9acaea88a42f029527110ece34371c9c2bae4b2cc"} {"question" "q-96662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040896/state.json" "file_sha256" "10bda9637715baf9cdfb337ccfa9d74b08b2b7bcef1833d0feb2b5c50a042eee"} {"question" "q-96662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/mul